      "writtenOn": "2022-10-17T14:07:13Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "C doesn\u0027t support declaring a function using a function typedef. (And also has the (void) wart.)\nBut I like the typedef because it gives me type safety in launcher/main.cpp, which is known to be C++.\nI guess I should add the typedef, even if I don\u0027t use it in the C version.",
      "parentUuid": "85ba49d0_a6d15988",
      "revId": "40c1e0d32648b4bac4d483ba3cef472dd2011889",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
